<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huaiyang District</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huaiyang is a district of Zhoukou in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It occupies the site of Wanqiu, capital of the State of Chen, and later of the city of Chen, which briefly served as the capital of Chu after 278 BCE and was the base of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-sheng">Chen Sheng</a>'s revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> in 209 BCE. It is a traditional centre of the cult of the mythical ancestor Fuxi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huaiyang-district.jpg" alt="Huaiyang District" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muqing112233 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mud_dog.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
